# Language

The user may write in **Spanish**. All **product-facing copy** and **project artifacts** stay in **English**.

## English (required)

- UI labels, buttons, headings, empty states, tooltips, placeholders
- Error and success messages shown in the app
- Code identifiers, comments, commit messages, PR titles/bodies
- Docs in the repo (`AGENTS.md`, migrations comments, etc.)

## Spanish (allowed)

- Chat with the user (replies can be in Spanish if they wrote in Spanish)
- User-provided domain content (company names, contact names, notes)

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Spanish UI copy
<PageTitle label="Contactos" />
<DataTable.Col label="Fecha de creación" />

// ✅ GOOD
<PageTitle label="Contacts" />
<DataTable.Col label="Created" />
```

When editing existing Spanish UI strings, prefer converting them to English unless the user explicitly asks for Spanish localization.
